# dev-notes.31 — runtime-public-entrypoint-contract-v1

Date: 2026-06-08
Branch/slice: runtime-public-entrypoint-contract-v1

## Purpose

Add a static public-entrypoint contract guard so `runtime.mjs` remains a thin public API/composition root after the parent-runtime and Worker Layout Option C modularization work.

This branch is intended to close the current modularization arc for now. It protects the current entrypoint boundary against future casual re-bloating instead of performing another production extraction.

## Scope

Added:

```text
tests/smokeTestRuntimePublicEntrypointContract.mjs
docs/dev-notes.31
```

Modified:

```text
none
```

## Public entrypoint contract guarded

The new smoke test statically checks that `runtime.mjs` exports exactly:

```text
cancelPrompt
initModel
prompt
resetModel
resetSession
shutdownRuntime
```

It also checks that `runtime.mjs` continues to act as a composition root by referencing the expected runtime coordinator/helper modules while avoiding direct worker/native/model execution dependencies.

## Important test design note

The smoke test intentionally does not import `runtime.mjs`. Current `runtime.mjs` wires the worker protocol router at module load, and `workerBridge.mjs` creates the worker when `onWorkerMessage()` is called without an existing worker. A static source-text contract test avoids starting a worker and avoids requiring `node-llama-cpp` for this guard branch.

## Protected boundaries

The test guards these entrypoint boundaries:

```text
runtime.mjs remains the stable public runtime API entrypoint
runtime.mjs remains a composition root, not a parent-runtime dumping ground
workerBridge.mjs continues targeting ./llama_worker/llama.mjs
llama_worker/llama.mjs remains the worker entrypoint/composition root
executable non-legacy source does not depend on inference.mjs
runtime.mjs does not directly import node-llama-cpp or llama_worker internals
```

## Non-goals

This branch does not include:

```text
production runtime behavior changes
production worker behavior changes
public API changes
scheduler changes
config/configOverride changes
prompt/output semantic changes
model identity/path changes
lifecycle behavior changes
cancellation behavior changes
cleanup refactors
optimization work
new feature work
real-runtime dependency requirements
```

## Propagation review

No runtime fixture file lists were changed or required. The new smoke test reads source files directly and imports only Node built-ins.

No production imports changed. No worker imports changed. No package entrypoints changed. No test fixture architecture changed.

## Validation notes

Recommended validation for this branch:

```bash
find . -name '*.mjs' -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 -n1 node --check
node ./tests/tools/checkWorkerImportCycles.mjs
node ./tests/tools/checkRuntimeFixtureCoverage.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestRuntimePublicEntrypointContract.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerProtocolContract.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerStreamOrdering.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerModelPathImmutability.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerModelDisposalPolicy.mjs
```

Real-runtime testing is not required if this branch remains test/docs only.

## Caveats

This is a static guard, not behavioral proof. It catches entrypoint/export/wiring drift and stale `inference.mjs` executable references, but it does not replace lifecycle, cancellation, shutdown, stream, or real-runtime smoke suites when production runtime behavior changes.

GitHub remains source truth unless Michael says otherwise. Direct ref-qualified GitHub source inspection should still be used after upload before claiming repo-verified status.

## Future work not included

Future work should be feature-specific, bug-specific, tool-calling-specific, or explicitly approved cleanup/optimization. Further production extraction from `runtime.mjs` should not happen by inertia.
